+Physics shows the same difficulty at the largest scale. Quantum mechanics and general relativity each describe their own domain with great precision, and each speaks in its own terms, so joining them into one account remains an open question. Pattern Arithmetic does not address that question, and nothing here applies to either theory. The refusal to Mix across differing directions (\S\ref{subsec:mix_scattered_open}) is a small case of the same problem, settled by declining rather than by a found rule, and it is a reason to begin at a narrow scale and test it honestly.
 
